> just got started on nethack, but can't seem to get further than the
> 5th or 6th level. anybody got tips? :D

Nethack is not like, say, Gothic. It's not about leveling or farming,
it's about surviving. You survive by enhancing your armor class
through wearing non-cursed, enchanted, lightweight armor, getting
important resistances as soon as possible (poision, cold, fire), and
-- most important -- avioiding dangerous situations and monsters. If
you enter the Gnomish Mines, and the level is dark and you don't have
a lamp, leave. It's dangerous. Get Telepathy from eating a floating
eye, and put on a blindfold in every level to check it for dangerous
monsters (soldier ants, rothes, mumaks, unicorns, many killer bees),
and if there's too many of them, leave and play another branch first
(means, switch between the mines and the main dungeon). #pray if in
trouble, and if there's only a 10% chance you might die and you have
an item that will save you (healing pot etc.) *use it*. Collect items
that might save you in dangerous situations (scroll of teleport, ...),
and if you are in a dangerous situation, use them and don't wait for a
more dangerous one. Go back to explored, safe areas and regenerate if
below 1/2 of your hitpoints. Explore each level fully before
descending further. Don't try to level up quick, but other way round
-- keep your experience level moderate (roughly equivalent to the
dungeon level is quite much already), and let your pet kill stuff,
it's stronger than you. That way, generated monsters will be much
weaker, and you can buy protection for less money. Engrave Elbereth
frequently to avoid taking damage, then throw or shoot stuff, or cast
spells. Use hit-and-run tactics against slow monsters like Gnomes. And
-- learn from your mistakes. :)

